<title>GREECE: GREECE RAISES 220BLN DRS FROM SALE OF 2YR ZEROS.</title>
<headline>GREECE RAISES 220BLN DRS FROM SALE OF 2YR ZEROS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Greek finance ministry raised about 220 billion drachmas from its first ever sale of two-year zero coupon notes, a government source told Reuters.</p>
<p>&quot;The two-year zero coupon bonds sold very well,&quot; the source said. &quot;We are very satisfied with the public's reception.&quot;</p>
<p>The bonds carry a gross yield-to-maturity of 10.30 percent.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
